>> title: Braised Short Ribs, Slow Cooker
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, wine, braise, sunday dinner, slow cooker, crock pot
>> counters: The Slow Cooker
>> dish: braised-short-ribs
>> kit: Slow Cooker
>> aka: short ribs, braised beef short ribs, slow cooker short ribs, crockpot short ribs, red wine short ribs
>> servings: 6
>> time: 7 hr 35 min
>> slack: forgiving — the ribs are done at six hours and hold at eight without minding; the sauce is the part with no room at all, and it comes out of this pot loose every single time unless you reduce it in a pan
>> step.2: season, both sides
>> step.3: sear 12 min in a skillet, in batches
>> step.4: soften, deglaze the skillet clean
>> step.5: braise on low, 7 hr
>> step.6: reduce in a wide pan, 15 min

Written for low, seven hours. Three cups of liquid where the oven version takes seven — and even so the sauce comes out thinner than the plain way, because an oven braise spends three hours quietly reducing and this spends seven hours reducing nothing at all. The last operation is not optional and it does not happen in the machine.

Season @bone-in beef short ribs{5%lb}(2.3 kg; cut in 3-in lengths) with @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, @black pepper{2%tsp}.

Sear @&(~1)seasoned short ribs{} in @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} in a #skillet{} for ~sear{12%min}, in batches, on the meat faces and the fat cap.

Soften @yellow onions{2%large}(chopped), @carrots{2%large}(chopped), @celery{2%ribs}(chopped), @garlic{6%cloves}, @tomato paste{3%Tbs} in the same skillet with @&(~1)seared short ribs{}, then pour in @dry red wine{1 1/2%cup}(355 mL) and scrape the base clean.

Slow cook @&(~1)pot{} with @beef stock{1 1/2%cup}(355 mL), @thyme{6%sprigs} in a #slow cooker{} on low for ~slow cook{7%hr}, lid on and left alone.

Reduce the liquid from @&(~1)short ribs{} in a wide #saucepan{} for ~reduce{15%min}, with the ribs lifted out and kept warm, until it coats a spoon — then pour it back over them.
